IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`
IMPORT `sgba-sched`
IMPORT `sgba-p1-defs`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 3 (LICENSING SCHEME, ss 5 to 7) and PART 4 (BROADCASTING SERVICES, ss 8 to 19).
-- s 8(1) and the licence-holding facts are dated (they depend on the Second Schedule); every other rule states the
-- 2024 consolidation. Judgments the Act gives to the Authority ("as the Authority may determine", "is satisfied")
-- are asked as plain facts, never guessed.

§ `Part 3 -- Licensing scheme`

-- src:986 | 5.—(1) The Authority may grant the following licences:
-- src:987 | (a) broadcasting licences;
-- src:988 | (b) broadcasting apparatus licences.
@ref s 5(1) (src:986-988)
-- The two licences the Authority may grant by this subsection. A class licence is determined by notification under s 9 and is "a broadcasting licence".
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of licence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) the Authority may grant a licence of this kind by this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a broadcasting licence granted under section 8` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a class licence determined under section 9` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a broadcasting apparatus licence granted under section 20` THEN TRUE

-- src:989 | (2) The Authority may grant licences under subsection (1) in such
-- src:990 | categories as the Authority may determine are appropriate for the
-- src:991 | regulation of the broadcasting industry.
@ref s 5(2) (src:989-991)
-- Whether a category is appropriate for the regulation of the broadcasting industry is the Authority's determination.
GIVEN `the Authority has determined the category to be appropriate for the regulation of the broadcasting industry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(2) the Authority may grant a licence in this category` MEANS
    `the Authority has determined the category to be appropriate for the regulation of the broadcasting industry`

-- src:998 | 6.—(1) The Authority may issue and from time to time review —
-- src:1000 | (a) Codes of Practice relating to standards of programmes and
-- src:1001 | advertisements broadcast by licensees; and
-- src:1003 | (b) Codes of Practice relating to broadcast standards required
-- src:1004 | to be maintained by licensees.
@ref s 6(1) (src:998-1004)
GIVEN `it relates to standards of programmes and advertisements broadcast by licensees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to broadcast standards required to be maintained by licensees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) the Authority may issue this Code of Practice` MEANS
    `it relates to standards of programmes and advertisements broadcast by licensees` OR `it relates to broadcast standards required to be maintained by licensees`

-- src:1006 | (2) Any provision in any Code of Practice that is inconsistent with
-- src:1007 | any regulations is, to the extent of the inconsistency —
-- src:1009 | (a) to have effect subject to the regulations; or
-- src:1011 | (b) where appropriate, having regard to the regulations, to
-- src:1012 | have no effect.
@ref s 6(2) (src:1006-1012)
-- Inconsistent provision: it has effect subject to the regulations, or, where appropriate, has no effect.
GIVEN `the provision is inconsistent with regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) the provision of the Code has effect subject to the regulations, to the extent of the inconsistency` MEANS
    IF `the provision is inconsistent with regulations` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1014 | (3) The Authority may in any licence exempt any licensee from any
-- src:1015 | provision in a Code of Practice generally or for any time that the
-- src:1016 | Authority may specify.
@ref s 6(3) (src:1014-1016)
GIVEN `the exemption is written in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(3) the licensee is exempt from the provision of the Code of Practice` MEANS
    `the exemption is written in the licence`

-- src:1020 | 7.—(1) A licence must not be transferred to any other person
-- src:1021 | without the prior written consent of the Authority to the transfer to
-- src:1022 | that person.
@ref s 7(1) (src:1020-1022)
GIVEN `the Authority has given its prior written consent to the transfer to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the licence may be transferred to another person` MEANS
    `the Authority has given its prior written consent to the transfer to that person`

-- src:1024 | (2) Any purported transfer of any licence is for all purposes void
-- src:1025 | and of no effect.
@ref s 7(2) (src:1024-1025)
-- LITERAL READING: any purported transfer is void. A second reading, that only a purported transfer made without the
-- consent s 7(1) requires is void, is in the fork register (F-BA-02) and is the next function.
GIVEN `a transfer of the licence is purported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the purported transfer is void and of no effect, read literally` MEANS
    IF `a transfer of the licence is purported` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1020 | 7.—(1) A licence must not be transferred to any other person
-- src:1021 | without the prior written consent of the Authority to the transfer to
-- src:1022 | that person.
-- src:1024 | (2) Any purported transfer of any licence is for all purposes void
-- src:1025 | and of no effect.
@ref s 7(1) read with (2): the consent reading (src:1020-1025)
GIVEN `a transfer of the licence is purported` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has given its prior written consent to the transfer to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the purported transfer is void, on the reading that only a transfer without consent is` MEANS
    IF `a transfer of the licence is purported` THEN JUST (NOT `the Authority has given its prior written consent to the transfer to that person`) ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 4 -- Broadcasting services`

-- src:1033 | 8.—(1) A person must not provide any licensable broadcasting
-- src:1034 | service in or from Singapore without a broadcasting licence granted
-- src:1035 | by the Authority under this section or granted under section 9.
@ref s 8(1) (src:1033-1035)
-- Dated: whether the service is licensable depends on the Second Schedule. NOTHING outside the window of the deposited text.
-- "granted under this section or granted under section 9": a class licence determined under s 9 that applies to the provider counts.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
      `it is or has ever been an online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides the service in or from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a broadcasting licence granted by the Authority under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a class licence determined under section 9 applies to the person's service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the person provides a licensable broadcasting service without the licence the subsection requires, on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(1) the broadcasting service is a licensable broadcasting service on` d s `it is or has ever been an online communication service`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST licensable THEN JUST (licensable AND `the person provides the service in or from Singapore` AND (NOT `the person holds a broadcasting licence granted by the Authority under section 8`) AND (NOT `a class licence determined under section 9 applies to the person's service`))

-- src:1037 | (2) Every broadcasting licence (other than a class licence) granted
-- src:1038 | by the Authority must be in such form and for such period and may
-- src:1039 | contain such terms and conditions as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 8(2) (src:1037-1039)
GIVEN `it is a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has determined its form, period and terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) the licence is in the form, for the period and on the terms the Authority determined` MEANS
    IF `it is a class licence` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the Authority has determined its form, period and terms and conditions`

-- src:1044 | (3) The Authority may require any licensee to pay a fee on the grant
-- src:1045 | of the licence or such periodic fees while the licence is in force or
-- src:1046 | both of such amount as the Authority may determine by or under the
-- src:1047 | licence.
@ref s 8(3) (src:1044-1047)
GIVEN `the Authority has required the fee, on grant or periodically or both, of the amount it determined by or under the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the licensee must pay the fee` MEANS
    `the Authority has required the fee, on grant or periodically or both, of the amount it determined by or under the licence`

-- src:1049 | (4) Without limiting subsection (2), conditions attached to a
-- src:1050 | free‑to‑air licence granted under this section may include —
-- src:1052 | (a) a condition requiring the licensee to broadcast any
-- src:1053 | programmes that the Authority may require and at such
-- src:1054 | time, or within such period and on such broadcasting
-- src:1055 | service as the Authority may specify;
-- src:1057 | (b) a condition prohibiting or restricting, in a manner specified
-- src:1058 | in the licence, the broadcasting by the licensee of
-- src:1059 | advertising material which is of a class or description so
-- src:1060 | specified;
-- src:1062 | (c) the right of the Authority in the public interest to make
-- src:1063 | modifications to any condition of the licence during the
-- src:1064 | period to which the licence relates;
-- src:1066 | (d) a condition requiring the licensee to provide a performance
-- src:1067 | bond to secure compliance by the licensee with any
-- src:1068 | condition attached to the licence;
-- src:1070 | (e) broadcast requirements, including conditions relating to
-- src:1071 | the assignment and use of frequencies, channel capacities
-- src:1072 | and coverage;
-- src:1074 | (f) a condition requiring the payment by the licensee of
-- src:1075 | royalties, licence fees, spectrum utilisation fees and other
-- src:1076 | fees and charges as may be prescribed;
-- src:1078 | (g) a condition requiring the broadcasting of programmes in
-- src:1079 | any language that may be specified, and the periods and
-- src:1080 | duration of such broadcast; and
-- src:1082 | (h) conditions imposing controls and restrictions, directly or
-- src:1083 | indirectly, on the creation, holding or disposal of shares in
-- src:1084 | the licensee or its shareholders or interests in the
-- src:1085 | undertaking of the licensee or any part thereof.
@ref s 8(4)(a) to (h) (src:1049-1085)
GIVEN `it requires the licensee to broadcast programmes the Authority requires, at the time or within the period and on the service the Authority specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it prohibits or restricts, in a manner the licence specifies, advertising material of a class the licence specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it gives the Authority the right in the public interest to modify a condition of the licence during its period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the licensee to provide a performance bond` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a broadcast requirement, including conditions on the assignment and use of frequencies, channel capacities and coverage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires payment of royalties, licence fees, spectrum utilisation fees and other fees and charges as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires broadcasting of programmes in a specified language, and the periods and duration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it imposes controls and restrictions on the creation, holding or disposal of shares in the licensee or its shareholders or interests in its undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the condition may be attached to a free-to-air licence granted under section 8` MEANS
    IF `it requires the licensee to broadcast programmes the Authority requires, at the time or within the period and on the service the Authority specifies`
       OR `it prohibits or restricts, in a manner the licence specifies, advertising material of a class the licence specifies`
       OR `it gives the Authority the right in the public interest to modify a condition of the licence during its period`
       OR `it requires the licensee to provide a performance bond`
       OR `it is a broadcast requirement, including conditions on the assignment and use of frequencies, channel capacities and coverage`
       OR `it requires payment of royalties, licence fees, spectrum utilisation fees and other fees and charges as may be prescribed`
       OR `it requires broadcasting of programmes in a specified language, and the periods and duration`
       OR `it imposes controls and restrictions on the creation, holding or disposal of shares in the licensee or its shareholders or interests in its undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1090 | (5) The Authority may require any licensee to pay a charge of such
-- src:1091 | amount as the Authority may determine for the late payment of any
-- src:1092 | royalty, fee or charge payable by that licensee to the Authority.
@ref s 8(5) (src:1090-1092)
GIVEN `the Authority has required a charge, of the amount it determined, for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge payable by the licensee to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) the licensee must pay the late payment charge` MEANS
    `the Authority has required a charge, of the amount it determined, for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge payable by the licensee to the Authority`

-- src:1096 | (6) Every amount collected before the date of commencement of
-- src:1097 | the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- src:1098 | purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any royalty, fee or
-- src:1099 | charge shall be deemed to be and always to have been validly
-- src:1100 | collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or
-- src:1101 | maintained in any court of law on account of or in respect of any such
-- src:1102 | collection.
@ref s 8(6) (src:1096-1102)
-- The deeming and the bar on proceedings concern amounts collected before the commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous
-- Amendments) Act 2008. The commencement of that Act is 1 April 2024: S 244/2024 appoints it for the Act except ss 9 and 12, and the only earlier appointment, S 128/2008 (18 March 2008),
-- was cancelled by S 129/2008 (fork F-BA-09, answered by those texts; `sgba-versions-later.l4` computes the date).
-- Here, on the 2024 text, whether the amount was collected before that commencement is still asked as a plain fact.
GIVEN `the amount was collected, or purportedly collected, as a charge for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge before the commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(6) the amount is deemed always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings lie on account of the collection` MEANS
    IF `the amount was collected, or purportedly collected, as a charge for the late payment of a royalty, fee or charge before the commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1108 | 9.—(1) The Authority may, by notification in the Gazette,
-- src:1109 | determine a class licence (being a broadcasting licence) for the
-- src:1110 | provision of such subscription broadcasting services and other
-- src:1111 | licensable broadcasting services as the Authority may specify.
@ref s 9(1) (src:1108-1111)
GIVEN `the Authority has determined it by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a subscription broadcasting service or another licensable broadcasting service the Authority specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the class licence has been determined` MEANS
    `the Authority has determined it by notification in the Gazette` AND `it is for a subscription broadcasting service or another licensable broadcasting service the Authority specified`

-- src:1113 | (2) The Authority may include in a class licence any conditions that
-- src:1114 | it thinks fit.
@ref s 9(2) (src:1113-1114)
GIVEN `the Authority thinks the condition fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the Authority may include the condition in a class licence` MEANS
    `the Authority thinks the condition fit`

-- src:1116 | (3) Different conditions may be specified for —
-- src:1118 | (a) different categories of licensable broadcasting services;
-- src:1119 | and
-- src:1121 | (b) different types of such services.
@ref s 9(3) (src:1116-1121)
GIVEN `the conditions are for a different category or a different type of licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(3) different conditions may be specified` MEANS
    `the conditions are for a different category or a different type of licensable broadcasting service`

-- src:1123 | (4) Without limiting the conditions that may be imposed, the
-- src:1124 | Authority may impose a condition on a class licence requiring the
-- src:1125 | licensee to comply with a Code of Practice that is applicable to the
-- src:1126 | licensee or designed to ensure that a breach of a condition of the class
-- src:1127 | licence by the licensee does not recur.
@ref s 9(4) (src:1123-1127)
GIVEN `the condition requires the licensee to comply with a Code of Practice applicable to it, or designed to ensure that a breach does not recur` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(4) the Authority may impose the condition on a class licence` MEANS
    `the condition requires the licensee to comply with a Code of Practice applicable to it, or designed to ensure that a breach does not recur`

-- src:1131 | 10.—(1) The Authority may modify the conditions of a
-- src:1132 | broadcasting licence (other than a class licence) in accordance with
-- src:1133 | this section.
@ref s 10(1) (src:1131-1133)
GIVEN `it is a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the Authority may modify the conditions of the licence under section 10` MEANS
    NOT `it is a class licence`

-- src:1138 | (2) Before making any modification to the conditions of a
-- src:1139 | broadcasting licence under this section, the Authority must give
-- src:1140 | notice to the broadcasting licensee —
-- src:1142 | (a) stating that it proposes to make the modification in the
-- src:1143 | manner specified in the notice and (except if the
-- src:1144 | modification results from a contravention by the licensee
-- src:1145 | as described in section 12(1)(a) or any other default of the
-- src:1146 | licensee) the compensation payable (if any) for any
-- src:1147 | damage caused by the modification; and
-- src:1149 | (b) specifying the time (being at least 28 days from the date of
-- src:1150 | service of notice on the licensee) within which written
-- src:1151 | representations with respect to the proposed modification
-- src:1152 | may be made.
@ref s 10(2) (src:1138-1152)
GIVEN `the modification results from a contravention by the licensee as described in section 12(1)(a) or any other default of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the proposed modification in the manner specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the compensation payable, if any, for any damage caused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a time for written representations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the date of service of the notice to the end of that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the notice is a notice the Authority must give before modifying` MEANS
    `the notice states the proposed modification in the manner specified`
    AND (`the modification results from a contravention by the licensee as described in section 12(1)(a) or any other default of the licensee` OR `the notice states the compensation payable, if any, for any damage caused`)
    AND `the notice specifies a time for written representations`
    AND `the days from the date of service of the notice to the end of that time` AT LEAST 28

-- src:1154 | (3) Upon receiving any written representation mentioned in
-- src:1155 | subsection (2)(b), the Authority must consider the representation
-- src:1156 | and may —
-- src:1158 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:1160 | (b) amend the proposed modification or compensation payable
-- src:1161 | in accordance with the representation, or otherwise,
-- src:1163 | and, in either event, must thereupon issue a direction in writing to the
-- src:1164 | broadcasting licensee requiring that effect be given to the proposed
-- src:1165 | modification specified in the notice or to such modification as
-- src:1166 | subsequently amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
@ref s 10(3) (src:1154-1166)
GIVEN `the Authority has received a written representation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(3) the Authority must issue a direction in writing giving effect to the proposed modification, or the modification as amended` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has received a written representation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1168 | (4) Any broadcasting licensee aggrieved by a decision of the
-- src:1169 | Authority under subsection (3) may, within 14 days of receiving the
-- src:1170 | direction, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 10(4) (src:1168-1170)
GIVEN `the days since the licensee received the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the licensee may still appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` MEANS
    `the days since the licensee received the direction` AT MOST 14

-- src:1172 | (5) The Authority must not enforce a direction given under
-- src:1173 | subsection (3) —
-- src:1175 | (a) during the period mentioned in subsection (4); and
-- src:1177 | (b) while the broadcasting licensee’s appeal is under
-- src:1178 | consideration by the Minister.
@ref s 10(5) (src:1172-1178)
GIVEN `the period for appeal under section 10(4) is running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee's appeal is under consideration by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the Authority must not enforce the direction` MEANS
    `the period for appeal under section 10(4) is running` OR `the licensee's appeal is under consideration by the Minister`

-- src:1180 | (6) If no written representation is received by the Authority within
-- src:1181 | the time specified in subsection (2) or if any written representation
-- src:1182 | made under that subsection is withdrawn, the Authority may
-- src:1187 | immediately carry out the modification as specified in the notice
-- src:1188 | given under that subsection.
@ref s 10(6) (src:1180-1188)
GIVEN `no written representation was received within the time specified, or any representation made was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(6) the Authority may immediately carry out the modification specified in the notice` MEANS
    `no written representation was received within the time specified, or any representation made was withdrawn`

-- src:1191 | 11. The Authority may, by notification in the Gazette —
-- src:1192 | (a) modify the conditions specified in any class licence; or
-- src:1193 | (b) specify additional conditions of any class licence.
@ref s 11 (src:1191-1193)
-- Both limbs are the Authority's powers by notification in the Gazette; for a class licensee they mean the conditions can change.
GIVEN `the Authority has modified a condition of the class licence, or specified an additional condition, by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11 the class licence conditions are as modified or added to` MEANS
    `the Authority has modified a condition of the class licence, or specified an additional condition, by notification in the Gazette`

-- src:1197 | 12.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:1199 | (a) a broadcasting licensee is contravening, or has
-- src:1200 | contravened, any of the conditions of its licence, any
-- src:1201 | relevant Code of Practice, any of the provisions of this Act
-- src:1202 | or the regulations or any direction issued by the Minister or
-- src:1203 | the Authority to, or applicable to, the licensee;
-- src:1205 | (b) a broadcasting licensee has gone into compulsory or
-- src:1206 | voluntary liquidation other than for the purpose of
-- src:1207 | amalgamation or reconstruction;
-- src:1209 | (c) a broadcasting licensee has made any assignment to, or
-- src:1210 | composition with, its creditors; or
-- src:1212 | (d) the public interest or the security of Singapore so requires,
-- src:1214 | the Authority may, by written notice and without any compensation,
-- src:1215 | do either or both of the following:
-- src:1217 | (e) cancel the licence or suspend the licence for any period that
-- src:1218 | the Authority thinks fit and, in the case of a class licensee,
-- src:1219 | cancel or suspend the application of the class licence in
-- src:1220 | respect of the class licensee for any period that the
-- src:1221 | Authority thinks fit;
-- src:1223 | (f) require the payment of a fine of such amount as the
-- src:1224 | Authority thinks fit.
@ref s 12(1) (src:1197-1224)
-- The Authority's satisfaction is the Authority's: asked as four plain facts.
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee is contravening or has contravened a condition of its licence, a relevant Code of Practice, a provision of this Act or the regulations, or a direction of the Minister or the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee has gone into compulsory or voluntary liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee has made an assignment to, or composition with, its creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the public interest or the security of Singapore so requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the Authority may by written notice and without compensation cancel or suspend the licence, or require a fine of an amount it thinks fit, or both` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee is contravening or has contravened a condition of its licence, a relevant Code of Practice, a provision of this Act or the regulations, or a direction of the Minister or the Authority`
    OR `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee has gone into compulsory or voluntary liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`
    OR `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee has made an assignment to, or composition with, its creditors`
    OR `the Authority is satisfied that the public interest or the security of Singapore so requires`

-- src:1226 | (2) Any person who is aggrieved by any decision of the Authority
-- src:1227 | under this section may, within 14 days of receiving the notice
-- src:1228 | mentioned in subsection (1), appeal to the Minister whose decision is
-- src:1229 | final.
@ref s 12(2) (src:1226-1229)
GIVEN `the days since the person received the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the aggrieved person may still appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` MEANS
    `the days since the person received the notice` AT MOST 14

-- src:1234 | (3) In this section, “Code of Practice” includes —
-- src:1236 | (a) a code of practice issued by the Authority under section 61
-- src:1237 | of the Info‑communications Media Development
-- src:1238 | Authority Act 2016; and
-- src:1240 | (b) a code of practice issued under section 17 of the Media
-- src:1241 | Development Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 172,
-- src:1242 | 2003 Revised Edition) before the repeal of that Act by
-- src:1243 | the Info‑communications Media Development Authority
-- src:1244 | Act 2016.
@ref s 12(3) (src:1234-1244)
GIVEN `it is a code of practice issued by the Authority under section 61 of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a code of practice issued under section 17 of the Media Development Authority of Singapore Act before that Act was repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(3) Code of Practice includes this code` MEANS
    IF `it is a code of practice issued by the Authority under section 61 of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` OR `it is a code of practice issued under section 17 of the Media Development Authority of Singapore Act before that Act was repealed`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1250 | 13.—(1) Every broadcasting licensee must comply with the Codes
-- src:1251 | of Practice relating to standards of programmes and advertisements
-- src:1252 | and broadcast standards.
@ref s 13(1) (src:1250-1252)
GIVEN `the licensee complies with the Codes of Practice relating to standards of programmes and advertisements and broadcast standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the licensee does what the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the licensee complies with the Codes of Practice relating to standards of programmes and advertisements and broadcast standards`

-- src:1254 | (2) A broadcasting licensee must not allow to be transmitted a
-- src:1255 | broadcasting service other than in accordance with —
-- src:1257 | (a) any broadcast standards specified in any regulations or
-- src:1258 | Code of Practice; or
-- src:1260 | (b) any condition which may be incorporated in its
-- src:1261 | broadcasting licence.
@ref s 13(2) (src:1254-1261)
GIVEN `the service is transmitted in accordance with broadcast standards specified in regulations or a Code of Practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is transmitted in accordance with a condition incorporated in the broadcasting licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(2) the licensee has not allowed a service to be transmitted otherwise than as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the service is transmitted in accordance with broadcast standards specified in regulations or a Code of Practice` AND `the service is transmitted in accordance with a condition incorporated in the broadcasting licence`

-- src:1265 | 14.—(1) A free-to-air licensee must provide broadcasting services
-- src:1266 | in such language as may be specified in its licence.
@ref s 14(1) (src:1265-1266)
GIVEN `the licensee provides broadcasting services in the language specified in its licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the free-to-air licensee does what the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the licensee provides broadcasting services in the language specified in its licence`

-- src:1268 | (2) Each free-to-air broadcasting service must be broadcast for at
-- src:1269 | least such number of hours during each day as may be specified in the
-- src:1270 | free-to-air licence.
@ref s 14(2) (src:1268-1270)
GIVEN `the hours broadcast each day` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours the free-to-air licence specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(2) the free-to-air broadcasting service is broadcast for at least the hours specified` MEANS
    `the hours broadcast each day` AT LEAST `the hours the free-to-air licence specifies`

-- src:1274 | 15.—(1) A broadcasting licensee must supply to the Authority on
-- src:1275 | demand any material, including the script thereof, which is intended
-- src:1276 | for broadcasting.
@ref s 15(1) (src:1274-1276)
GIVEN `the licensee supplied the material, including the script, which is intended for broadcasting, on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1) the licensee has supplied the material the Authority demanded` MEANS
    `the licensee supplied the material, including the script, which is intended for broadcasting, on demand`

-- src:1278 | (2) A broadcasting licensee who is required to supply material
-- src:1279 | under subsection (1) must —
-- src:1284 | (a) supply the material in such form as the Authority may
-- src:1285 | determine; or
-- src:1287 | (b) make available on demand without charge such equipment
-- src:1288 | as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 15(2) (src:1278-1288)
GIVEN `the licensee supplied the material in the form the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee made available on demand without charge the equipment the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2) the licensee required to supply material has complied` MEANS
    `the licensee supplied the material in the form the Authority determined` OR `the licensee made available on demand without charge the equipment the Authority determined`

-- src:1290 | (3) The Authority may, if it is satisfied that any programme
-- src:1291 | intended to be broadcast by a broadcasting licensee may be against
-- src:1292 | the public interest or order, national harmony or will offend against
-- src:1293 | decency, require the broadcasting licensee to pre-record the
-- src:1294 | programme and submit it to the Authority for approval before it is
-- src:1295 | broadcast.
@ref s 15(3) (src:1290-1295)
-- Whether the programme may be against the public interest or order, national harmony or offend decency is the Authority's satisfaction.
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the programme may be against the public interest or order, national harmony or will offend against decency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(3) the Authority may require the licensee to pre-record the programme and submit it for approval before it is broadcast` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the programme may be against the public interest or order, national harmony or will offend against decency`

-- src:1299 | 16.—(1) The Authority may issue directions in writing to a
-- src:1300 | broadcasting licensee requiring the licensee to take any action with
-- src:1301 | regard to the contents of programmes or advertisements or to
-- src:1302 | broadcast standards that the Authority considers necessary in order to
-- src:1303 | comply with the provisions of this Act, any relevant Code of Practice
-- src:1304 | and any condition attached to the broadcasting licence.
@ref s 16(1) (src:1299-1304)
GIVEN `the Authority considers the action necessary to comply with this Act, a relevant Code of Practice or a condition attached to the broadcasting licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1) the Authority may direct in writing that the licensee take the action with regard to programme or advertisement contents or broadcast standards` MEANS
    `the Authority considers the action necessary to comply with this Act, a relevant Code of Practice or a condition attached to the broadcasting licence`

-- src:1306 | (2) Directions issued under subsection (1) may include a direction
-- src:1307 | prohibiting a broadcasting licensee from broadcasting the whole or
-- src:1308 | any part of a programme or of any class of material.
@ref s 16(2) (src:1306-1308)
GIVEN `the direction prohibits broadcasting the whole or any part of a programme or of a class of material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) the direction is one the subsection allows to be included` MEANS
    IF `the direction prohibits broadcasting the whole or any part of a programme or of a class of material` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1310 | (3) Any broadcasting licensee and any other person responsible for
-- src:1311 | the broadcasting of any programme prohibited by a direction issued
-- src:1312 | under subsection (1) shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each
-- src:1313 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- src:1314 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 16(3) (src:1310-1314)
-- Each of the licensee and any other person responsible for broadcasting a prohibited programme is guilty. Punishment: s 16(3) itself.
GIVEN `the person is the broadcasting licensee or another person responsible for the broadcasting of a programme prohibited by a direction under section 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is the broadcasting licensee or another person responsible for the broadcasting of a programme prohibited by a direction under section 16(1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

GIVETH A Punishment
`s 16(3) the punishment` MEANS Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 20000, `imprisonment` IS `imprisonment not exceeding` 24, `daily fine` IS `no further daily fine is provided`, `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:1318 | 17. A broadcasting licensee must include, within the broadcasting
-- src:1319 | services required to be broadcast by it under its broadcasting licence,
-- src:1320 | any programmes provided by the Authority or the Government
-- src:1321 | through the Authority as may be required by the Authority under the
-- src:1322 | conditions of its licence, including —
-- src:1324 | (a) programmes for schools or other educational programmes;
-- src:1329 | (b) news and information programmes produced in Singapore
-- src:1330 | or elsewhere;
-- src:1332 | (c) arts and cultural programmes; and
-- src:1334 | (d) drama and sports programmes produced in Singapore.
@ref s 17 (src:1318-1334)
GIVEN `the Authority requires the programme under the conditions of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the programme is provided by the Authority, or by the Government through the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17 the licensee must include the programme within the services it is required to broadcast` MEANS
    `the Authority requires the programme under the conditions of the licence` AND `the programme is provided by the Authority, or by the Government through the Authority`

-- src:1318 | 17. A broadcasting licensee must include, within the broadcasting
-- src:1319 | services required to be broadcast by it under its broadcasting licence,
-- src:1320 | any programmes provided by the Authority or the Government
-- src:1321 | through the Authority as may be required by the Authority under the
-- src:1322 | conditions of its licence, including —
-- src:1324 | (a) programmes for schools or other educational programmes;
-- src:1329 | (b) news and information programmes produced in Singapore
-- src:1330 | or elsewhere;
-- src:1332 | (c) arts and cultural programmes; and
-- src:1334 | (d) drama and sports programmes produced in Singapore.
@ref s 17(a) to (d) (src:1318-1334)
GIVEN `it is a programme for schools or another educational programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a news and information programme produced in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an arts and cultural programme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a drama or sports programme produced in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 the programme is of a kind the section lists` MEANS
    IF `it is a programme for schools or another educational programme` OR `it is a news and information programme produced in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `it is an arts and cultural programme` OR `it is a drama or sports programme produced in Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1338 | 18.—(1) Programmes required under section 17 or pursuant to a
-- src:1339 | condition attached to a broadcasting licence to be broadcast by a
-- src:1340 | broadcasting licensee must be broadcast without charge to the
-- src:1341 | Authority or with such subsidy from the Authority as may be
-- src:1342 | provided in that broadcasting licence.
@ref s 18(1) (src:1338-1342)
GIVEN `it is broadcast without charge to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is broadcast with a subsidy the broadcasting licence provides for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18(1) the programme required under section 17 or by a licence condition is broadcast as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `it is broadcast without charge to the Authority` OR `it is broadcast with a subsidy the broadcasting licence provides for`

-- src:1344 | (2) A broadcasting licensee must, on the request of the Authority
-- src:1345 | and on receiving reasonable notice, make available to the Authority
-- src:1346 | without charge such part of its broadcasting apparatus as the
-- src:1347 | Authority may specify for the purpose of broadcasting programmes
-- src:1348 | required to be broadcast under section 17 or pursuant to a condition
-- src:1349 | attached to its broadcasting licence.
@ref s 18(2) (src:1344-1349)
GIVEN `the Authority has requested it and given reasonable notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee made the part of its broadcasting apparatus the Authority specified available without charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) the licensee has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has requested it and given reasonable notice` THEN JUST `the licensee made the part of its broadcasting apparatus the Authority specified available without charge` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1353 | 19.—(1) Despite anything in this Act but subject to this section, the
-- src:1354 | Authority may, by a direction in writing, require a broadcasting
-- src:1355 | licensee to provide for transmission and reception any broadcasting
-- src:1356 | service which is —
-- src:1358 | (a) provided by any other person for such transmission and
-- src:1359 | reception; and
-- src:1361 | (b) specified in its licence or is of a description so specified.
@ref s 19(1) (src:1353-1361)
GIVEN `the service is provided by another person for transmission and reception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is specified in the licence or is of a description so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the Authority may by a direction in writing require the licensee to provide the service for transmission and reception` MEANS
    `the service is provided by another person for transmission and reception` AND `the service is specified in the licence or is of a description so specified`

-- src:1363 | (2) Where the Authority gives a direction under this section, the
-- src:1364 | broadcasting licensee to whom the direction is given must comply
-- src:1365 | with the requirements of the direction until it is withdrawn.
@ref s 19(2) (src:1363-1365)
GIVEN `a direction under section 19 has been given and not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) the licensee must comply with the direction` MEANS
    `a direction under section 19 has been given and not withdrawn`

-- src:1367 | (3) Where it is proposed to give a direction under this section, the
-- src:1368 | Authority must give notice to the broadcasting licensee —
-- src:1370 | (a) stating that the Authority proposes to give directions in the
-- src:1371 | manner specified in the notice and the compensation
-- src:1376 | payable (if any) for the damage caused by the direction;
-- src:1377 | and
-- src:1379 | (b) specifying the time (being at least 28 days from the date the
-- src:1380 | notice is served on the broadcasting licensee) within which
-- src:1381 | written representations with respect to the proposed
-- src:1382 | directions may be made.
@ref s 19(3) (src:1367-1382)
GIVEN `the notice states the manner of the proposed directions and the compensation payable, if any, for the damage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from service of the notice to the end of the time for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) the notice is the notice the Authority must give before proposing the direction` MEANS
    `the notice states the manner of the proposed directions and the compensation payable, if any, for the damage` AND `the days from service of the notice to the end of the time for representations` AT LEAST 28

-- src:1384 | (4) Upon receiving any written representation mentioned in
-- src:1385 | subsection (3)(b), the Authority must consider the representation
-- src:1386 | and may —
-- src:1388 | (a) reject the representation; or
-- src:1390 | (b) amend the proposed direction or compensation payable in
-- src:1391 | accordance with the representation, or otherwise,
-- src:1393 | and, in either event, must thereupon issue a direction in writing to the
-- src:1394 | broadcasting licensee requiring that effect be given to the proposed
-- src:1395 | direction specified in the notice or to such direction as subsequently
-- src:1396 | amended by the Authority within a reasonable time.
@ref s 19(4) (src:1384-1396)
GIVEN `the Authority has received a written representation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) the Authority must issue a direction in writing giving effect to the proposed direction, or as amended` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has received a written representation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1398 | (5) Any broadcasting licensee aggrieved by a decision of the
-- src:1399 | Authority under subsection (4) may, within 14 days of receiving the
-- src:1400 | direction, appeal to the Minister whose decision is final.
@ref s 19(5) (src:1398-1400)
GIVEN `the days since the licensee received the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(5) the licensee may still appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final` MEANS
    `the days since the licensee received the direction` AT MOST 14

-- src:1402 | (6) The Authority must not enforce a direction given under
-- src:1403 | subsection (4) —
-- src:1405 | (a) during the period mentioned in subsection (5); and
-- src:1407 | (b) while the broadcasting licensee’s appeal is under
-- src:1408 | consideration by the Minister.
@ref s 19(6) (src:1402-1408)
GIVEN `the period for appeal under section 19(5) is running` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee's appeal is under consideration by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) the Authority must not enforce the direction` MEANS
    `the period for appeal under section 19(5) is running` OR `the licensee's appeal is under consideration by the Minister`

-- src:1410 | (7) If no written representation is received by the Authority within
-- src:1411 | the time specified in subsection (3) or if any written representation
-- src:1412 | made under that subsection is withdrawn, the Authority may
-- src:1413 | immediately give effect to the requirements of the direction given
-- src:1414 | under this section.
@ref s 19(7) (src:1410-1414)
GIVEN `no written representation was received within the time specified, or any representation made was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(7) the Authority may immediately give effect to the requirements of the direction` MEANS
    `no written representation was received within the time specified, or any representation made was withdrawn`
